From: PARP LZX <lzx-note@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: restart scored reclaim after moving a memcg to a passed bin

A memcg can be created before its final application prior arrives and thus be
placed in a high fallback bin.  During reclaim, moving a newly cold memcg to a
lower bin that has already been visited must restart the ordered scan.  Without
the restart, the current invocation can reclaim hot memcgs left in the high bin
before it ever observes the cold target.  lzx-note

---
 mm/vmscan.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@
 	int bin;
 	int first_bin;
+	bool restart_lower_bin = false; /* lzx-note */
 	struct lruvec *lruvec;
@@
 		if (parp_memcg_reclaim_bin_scored(memcg, &scored_bin) &&
 		    scored_bin != bin) {
 			parp_reclaim_bin_note_rebin();
 			op = MEMCG_LRU_REBIN;
+			/*
+			 * An entry can be online in a high fallback bin before its
+			 * application prior arrives.  If the refreshed cold score moves
+			 * it to a bin already passed by this cycle, continuing here would
+			 * reclaim the remaining hot entries first.  Rotate it, then restart
+			 * at bin zero so a late cold prediction takes effect in this reclaim
+			 * invocation rather than the next one. lzx-note
+			 */
+			if (scored_bin < bin)
+				restart_lower_bin = true;
 			rcu_read_lock();
+			if (restart_lower_bin)
+				break;
 			continue;
 		}
@@
 	mem_cgroup_put(memcg);
+	if (restart_lower_bin) {
+		restart_lower_bin = false;
+		bin = first_bin;
+		goto restart;
+	} /* lzx-note */
 
 	if (!is_a_nulls(pos))
-- 
